1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,830
Good morning. Can I help you?

2
00:00:01,830 --> 00:00:05,648
Yes. I've just been accepted on a course at the university

3
00:00:05,648 --> 00:00:10,160
and I'd like to try and arrange accommodation in the hall of residence.

4
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:11,560
Yes, certainly. Please sit down.

5
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:17,720
What I'll do is fill in a form with you to find out a little more about your preferences and so forth.

6
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:18,630
Thank you.

7
00:00:18,630 --> 00:00:21,860
So first of all, can I take your name?

8
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:23,340
It's Anu Bhatt.

9
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:25,000
Could you spell your name please?

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,510
Yes. A-N-U...B-H-A double T.

11
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:34,220
Thanks, and could I ask your date of birth?

12
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:37,760
31st March 1972.

13
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:40,000
Thank you. And where are you from?

14
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:40,740
India.

15
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:44,100
Oh right. And what will you be studying?

16
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:46,350
I'm doing a course in nursing.

17
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:51,000
Right, thank you. And how long would you want to stay in hall, do you think?

18
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,654
Well, it'll take three years but I'd only like to stay in hall for two.

19
00:00:56,654 --> 00:01:00,800
I'd like to think about living outside for the third year.

20
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:04,090
Fine. And what did you have in mind for catering?

21
00:01:04,090 --> 00:01:08,960
Do you want to cook for yourself or have all your meals provided, that's full board?

22
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,460
Is there something in between?

23
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:15,190
Yes. You can just have evening meal provided, which is half board.

24
00:01:15,190 --> 00:01:17,040
That's what I'd prefer.

25
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:19,550
Yes a lot of students opt for that.

26
00:01:19,550 --> 00:01:24,570
Now, with that in mind, do you have any special diet, anything we should know about?

27
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:27,390
Yes, I don't take red meat.

28
00:01:27,390 --> 00:01:29,500
No red meat.

29
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:34,140
Now, thinking about the room itself, we have a number of options.

30
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:37,660
You can have a single study bedroom or you can have a shared one.

31
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:40,180
These are both what we call simple rooms.

32
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:47,180
The other alternative is to opt for a single bedsit which actually has more space and better facilities.

33
00:01:47,180 --> 00:01:50,140
There's about 20 a week difference between them.

34
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:54,020
Well, actually my grant is quite generous

35
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:56,760
and I think the bedsit sounds the best option.

36
00:01:56,760 --> 00:02:00,810
Lovely. I'll put you down for that and we'll see what availability is like.

37
00:02:00,810 --> 00:02:05,180
Now can I ask some other personal details which we like to have on record?

38
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:06,450
Yes, of course.

39
00:02:06,450 --> 00:02:09,500
I wonder if you could let us know what your interests are.

40
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,450
This might help us get a closer match for placing you in a particular hall.

41
00:02:13,450 --> 00:02:17,370
Ummm. Well, I love the theatre.

42
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:18,400
Right.

43
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:22,350
And I enjoy sports, particularly badmintion.

44
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:24,339
That's worth knowing. Now, what we finish

45
00:02:24,339 --> 00:02:29,738
with on the form is really a list from you of what your priorities are in choosing a hall

46
00:02:29,738 --> 00:02:32,580
and we'll do our best to take these into account.

47
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:37,000
Well, the first thing is I'd prefer a hall

48
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,870
where there are other mature students. If possible.

49
00:02:39,870 --> 00:02:43,450
Yes, we do have halls which tend to cater for slightly older students.

50
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:48,580
Ummm and I'd prefer to be out of town.

51
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,480
That's actually very good for you

52
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:53,300
because we tend to have more vacancies in out-of-town halls.

53
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,550
Lucky!

54
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:56,890
Yes. Anything else?

55
00:02:56,890 --> 00:03:00,138
Well, I would like somewhere with a shared area.

56
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:05,550
A TV room for example, or something like that. It's a good way to socialise.

57
00:03:05,550 --> 00:03:06,410
It certainly is.

58
00:03:06,410 --> 00:03:07,460
That's it.

59
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:10,790
Now, we just need a contact telephone number for you.

60
00:03:10,790 --> 00:03:19,590
Sure, I'll just find it. It's double 67549.

61
00:03:19,590 --> 00:03:22,950
Great, so we'll be in contact with you as soon as possible...
